01:35:39.859 --> 01:35:41.192
Oh, shit.

01:35:41.318 --> 01:35:42.652
(WOMAN YELLING)

01:35:44.655 --> 01:35:47.490
You're under arrest!
She must have
used a pass key.

01:35:47.616 --> 01:35:48.908
I was polishing my shoes
in the closet

01:35:48.993 --> 01:35:50.577
when I noticed her
sneaking in, so I took her.

01:35:50.661 --> 01:35:51.911
What made you do it?
Who paid you off?

01:35:51.996 --> 01:35:53.371
Nobody! I'm the maid !

01:35:53.456 --> 01:35:55.290
You're just as much
a part of it as they are.

01:35:55.374 --> 01:35:56.666
Part of what?

01:35:56.751 --> 01:35:58.418
The goddamn dope ring.

01:35:58.502 --> 01:36:00.128
You must know
what's going on
in this hotel.

01:36:00.212 --> 01:36:01.880
Why do you think we're here?

01:36:01.964 --> 01:36:03.673
(STUTTERING)
I know you're the cops,

01:36:03.799 --> 01:36:06.259
but I thought
you were just here
for the convention.

01:36:06.343 --> 01:36:09.304
I swear. All I wanted to do
was clean up the room.

01:36:09.889 --> 01:36:12.098
I don't know
anything about no dope.

01:36:12.183 --> 01:36:13.683
Come on, baby.

01:36:13.768 --> 01:36:15.935
Don't try to tell us
you never heard
of the Grange Gorman.

01:36:16.020 --> 01:36:18.521
I swear to Jesus
I never heard of that stuff.

01:36:18.856 --> 01:36:20.523
Maybe she's telling the truth.

01:36:21.025 --> 01:36:22.776
Maybe she's not part of it.

01:36:22.860 --> 01:36:25.653
I swear I'm not. I swear.

01:36:28.741 --> 01:36:30.658
In that case,
maybe she can help.

01:36:30.743 --> 01:36:33.161
Oh, yes,
I'll help you all you want.

01:36:33.579 --> 01:36:34.996
I hate dope.

01:36:35.539 --> 01:36:36.623
So do we.

01:36:36.707 --> 01:36:38.583
I think we should
put her on the payroll,

01:36:39.084 --> 01:36:40.752
see what she comes up with.

01:36:40.836 --> 01:36:42.629
You think
you can handle it?
What?

01:36:42.713 --> 01:36:44.839
One phone call every day.

01:36:45.090 --> 01:36:46.674
Don't worry
if it doesn't add up.

01:36:47.009 --> 01:36:48.134
That's our problem.

01:36:48.219 --> 01:36:49.928
You'd pay me for that?

01:36:50.012 --> 01:36:51.888
You're damn right we would.

01:36:52.473 --> 01:36:55.558
But the first time
that you say anything
about this to anybody

01:36:55.684 --> 01:36:58.436
you will go straight to prison
for the rest of your life.

01:36:58.729 --> 01:36:59.854
What's your name?

01:36:59.939 --> 01:37:01.439
Alice.
Prove it!

01:37:02.817 --> 01:37:04.067
Okay.

01:37:04.401 --> 01:37:06.486
Just ring Linen Service
and ask for Alice.

01:37:06.570 --> 01:37:08.029
All right, Alice.

01:37:11.575 --> 01:37:15.578
You'll be contacted
by Inspector Rock,
Arthur Rock.

01:37:16.455 --> 01:37:18.122
He'll be posing
as a politician,

01:37:18.207 --> 01:37:19.874
but you'll have no problem
recognizing him.

01:37:19.959 --> 01:37:24.128
That's right, Inspector Rock
will pay you in cash.

01:37:24.213 --> 01:37:26.256
$1 ,000 on the ninth
of every month.

01:37:26.423 --> 01:37:29.342
Oh, Lord ! I'd do just about
anything for that.

01:37:29.426 --> 01:37:31.344
You and a lot
of other people.

01:37:31.428 --> 01:37:35.098
Come here. The password is,
"One hand washes the other."

01:37:35.266 --> 01:37:39.143
The minute you hear that,
you say, "I fear nothing."

01:37:39.436 --> 01:37:40.812
Say it.

01:37:40.896 --> 01:37:42.146
I fear nothing.
Say it again !

01:37:42.231 --> 01:37:43.648
I fear nothing !
Very good.

01:37:43.983 --> 01:37:45.400
Get the fuck out of here.

01:37:45.484 --> 01:37:47.652
Oh, yeah, listen.
Nice meeting you.

01:37:49.154 --> 01:37:50.697
Don't bother
to make up the room.

01:37:50.781 --> 01:37:54.075
Just leave a pile of towels
and soap outside the door
exactly at midnight.

01:37:54.159 --> 01:37:56.744
That way we won't
have to risk another

01:37:56.829 --> 01:37:58.413
one of these
little incidents, will we?

01:37:58.497 --> 01:38:00.164
Whatever you say, gentlemen.

01:38:00.249 --> 01:38:01.958
Thank God for decent people.

01:38:02.793 --> 01:38:04.961
DUKE ON TAPE: Say it again!
WOMAN: l fear nothing!

01:38:05.504 --> 01:38:06.838
DUKE NARRATING:
Terrible gibberish.

01:38:06.922 --> 01:38:09.757
Splintered memories looming up
out of the time fog.

01:38:10.134 --> 01:38:12.260
Just press play.

01:38:13.012 --> 01:38:15.013
DUKE ON TAPE: This is it,
the American Dream.

01:38:15.097 --> 01:38:16.097
Shit!

01:38:16.181 --> 01:38:17.557
We're sitting
on the main nerve right now.

01:38:17.641 --> 01:38:19.475
Yeah, don't get me started.

01:38:20.019 --> 01:38:23.771
The owner always wanted
to run away and join
the circus when he was a kid.

01:38:23.856 --> 01:38:26.024
Now the son of a bitch
owns the circus.

01:38:27.151 --> 01:38:30.445
Ah, man,
a real license to steal.

01:38:30.529 --> 01:38:31.905
Oh, yeah.

01:38:31.989 --> 01:38:33.781
The American Dream
come true, man.

01:38:33.866 --> 01:38:35.533
Pure Horatio Alger.

01:38:36.201 --> 01:38:38.453
Yeah. Welcome
to the happy place.

01:38:38.787 --> 01:38:39.913
(GRUNTING)

01:38:40.289 --> 01:38:43.875
Listen, let's get down
to brass tacks here.

01:38:44.376 --> 01:38:46.127
How much for the ape?

01:38:46.378 --> 01:38:48.463
MAN CHUCKLING:
How much you got?

01:38:48.839 --> 01:38:50.924
DUKE ON TAPE:
How much do you think
you'd take for the ape?

01:38:51.175 --> 01:38:53.259
Just wait here.
l'll be back.

01:38:53.344 --> 01:38:56.471
DUKE NARRATING: Madness.
lt made no sense at all.

01:38:56.555 --> 01:38:58.514
l desperately
needed the facts.

01:38:59.391 --> 01:39:00.516
(DUKE YELLING)

01:39:03.687 --> 01:39:05.271
(HARD ROCK MUSIC
PLAYING ON TAPE)

01:39:07.024 --> 01:39:08.900
What the fuck is going on?

01:39:08.984 --> 01:39:10.902
Where's the ape, man?
Where's the ape?

01:39:10.986 --> 01:39:13.363
MAN: Forget about it.
He attacked an old man.

01:39:13.530 --> 01:39:14.864
Bit off the head
of the bartender,

01:39:14.949 --> 01:39:17.659
then the cops came
and took him away.

01:39:19.328 --> 01:39:21.162
(GRUNTING)
Is that your car?

01:39:22.456 --> 01:39:23.706
(SHOUTING)

01:39:26.710 --> 01:39:28.336
Somebody stop them !

01:39:28.420 --> 01:39:30.046
DUKE: You poor fools
don't understand, do you?

01:39:30.130 --> 01:39:32.674
This car is property
of the World Bank.
That money goes to Italy.

01:39:32.758 --> 01:39:35.468
You can't put on a circus
without a tent.

01:39:35.552 --> 01:39:38.554
The top
is completely jammed.
You're right.

01:39:39.181 --> 01:39:40.556
There's something wrong
with the motor.

01:39:40.641 --> 01:39:42.600
We're all riders of the storm.

01:39:42.685 --> 01:39:45.728
Where are you,
you fucking monkey?
You can't do that!

01:39:48.148 --> 01:39:49.816
You people voted
for Hubert Humphrey.

01:39:49.900 --> 01:39:51.275
And you killed Jesus.

01:39:51.402 --> 01:39:54.195
DUKE: There was every reason
to believe that we'd been
heading for trouble,

01:39:54.279 --> 01:39:56.781
that we'd pushed
our luck a bit too far.

01:39:56.865 --> 01:39:59.617
Oh, gosh, shit! God !

01:40:01.787 --> 01:40:03.871
Right. Uh. . .

01:40:03.956 --> 01:40:05.957
The possibility

01:40:06.041 --> 01:40:08.793
of physical
and mental collapse

01:40:09.378 --> 01:40:11.587
is now very real.

01:40:12.214 --> 01:40:14.132
No sympathy for the devil.

01:40:14.717 --> 01:40:16.592
Keep that in mind.

01:40:16.927 --> 01:40:18.928
Uh, buy the ticket. . .

01:40:19.596 --> 01:40:22.015
Uh, take the ride.

01:40:23.183 --> 01:40:24.475
(WEEPING)

01:40:25.978 --> 01:40:27.478
Hey, there.

01:40:27.563 --> 01:40:30.106
You folks want to
buy some heroin?

01:40:30.566 --> 01:40:31.941
(GONZO WEEPING)

01:40:37.448 --> 01:40:39.824
Hey, honkies! Goddamn it!

01:40:39.908 --> 01:40:41.826
Pull ahead, will you?

01:40:41.910 --> 01:40:45.371
I want to sell you
some pure fucking scag !

01:40:45.456 --> 01:40:48.041
Cheap! The real stuff.

01:40:48.125 --> 01:40:51.753
I just got back from Vietnam.

01:40:57.217 --> 01:40:58.426
Scag.

01:41:00.637 --> 01:41:03.765
I want to sell you
some pure fucking scag.

01:41:03.974 --> 01:41:06.434
Shit! Fuck!

01:41:07.561 --> 01:41:11.397
Now hear me, you bastard !
Pull over! I'll kill you !

01:41:11.482 --> 01:41:12.982
MAN ON TAPE:
Pull over! Come on!

01:41:14.693 --> 01:41:16.402
Oh, shit. Oh, oh.

01:41:18.113 --> 01:41:19.655
(SLOW JAZZ MUSIC PLAYING)

01:41:24.953 --> 01:41:28.998
Okay. Let's see here.

01:41:36.423 --> 01:41:40.343
DUKE NARRATING:
The mentality of Las Vegas
is so grossly atavistic

01:41:40.427 --> 01:41:44.097
that a really massive crime
often slips by unrecognized.

01:41:45.224 --> 01:41:46.891
DUKE NARRATING:
lt was all over now.

01:41:47.268 --> 01:41:50.145
We'd abused every rule
that Vegas lived by.

01:41:50.855 --> 01:41:54.107
Threatening the locals,
abusing the tourists,

01:41:54.191 --> 01:41:56.151
terrifying the help.

01:41:56.235 --> 01:41:58.069
The only chance now, l felt

01:41:58.154 --> 01:42:01.156
was the possibility
that we'd gone to such excess

01:42:01.615 --> 01:42:04.284
that nobody in the position
to bring the hammer
down on us

01:42:04.368 --> 01:42:06.161
could possibly believe it.

01:42:06.746 --> 01:42:09.497
Fifteen minutes to get
my attorney to the airport,

01:42:10.124 --> 01:42:11.666
could we make it?

01:42:12.418 --> 01:42:14.252
Christ!

01:42:15.212 --> 01:42:16.755
No!

01:42:17.673 --> 01:42:18.923
Oh, fuck!

01:42:19.008 --> 01:42:20.967
Fuck.
Whoa, shit! Whoa, shit!

01:42:21.052 --> 01:42:23.511
Oh, God. Oh, God.
You son of a bitch !

01:42:23.596 --> 01:42:25.055
Oh, God.

01:42:25.681 --> 01:42:26.931
(SCREAMING)

01:42:26.974 --> 01:42:29.100
GONZO: You're going
the wrong way.
DUKE: The next left.

01:42:29.393 --> 01:42:30.393
GONZO: Stop!

01:42:30.478 --> 01:42:32.979
Go! Fuck!

01:42:37.193 --> 01:42:39.652
Take a right here.
Take a right here.

01:42:48.996 --> 01:42:51.623
GONZO: Goddamn it. We're lost.

01:42:52.458 --> 01:42:55.502
What are we doing
out here on this
godforsaken road?

01:42:56.295 --> 01:42:58.213
The airport's over there.

01:42:58.297 --> 01:43:01.132
Goddamn it! It's over there.

01:43:01.967 --> 01:43:03.885
I've never
missed a plane yet.

01:43:04.303 --> 01:43:05.637
(TIRES SCREECHING)

01:43:27.284 --> 01:43:28.660
Hold on !

01:43:34.625 --> 01:43:37.127
All right. I'm gonna drop you
right next to the plane.

01:43:37.211 --> 01:43:39.921
Fuck you. I'm gonna
have to take the blame.
They'll crucify me.

01:43:40.005 --> 01:43:41.548
Right here, right here.

01:43:41.632 --> 01:43:42.674
Ridiculous, man.

01:43:42.758 --> 01:43:46.761
Just say you were hitchhiking
to the airport,
and I picked you up.

01:43:46.846 --> 01:43:47.971
You bastard.

01:43:48.055 --> 01:43:49.222
Get out.

01:43:59.900 --> 01:44:01.985
Hey, hey! Hey, listen.

01:44:02.528 --> 01:44:04.779
Don't take any guff
from these swine.

01:44:05.030 --> 01:44:07.615
If you have
any trouble, remember,

01:44:07.825 --> 01:44:09.993
you can always send a telegram
to the right people.

01:44:10.077 --> 01:44:12.036
Yeah, explaining my position.

01:44:12.204 --> 01:44:14.205
Some asshole wrote
a poem about that once.

01:44:14.874 --> 01:44:17.834
Probably good advice,
if you have shit for brains.

01:44:19.462 --> 01:44:20.879
(GONZO LAUGHING)

01:44:24.258 --> 01:44:28.595
DUKE NARRATING: There he goes.
One of God's own prototypes.

01:44:29.430 --> 01:44:30.930
A high-powered mutant
of some kind

01:44:31.015 --> 01:44:33.224
never even considered
for mass production.

01:44:33.767 --> 01:44:35.310
Too weird to live,

01:44:35.561 --> 01:44:37.687
(GRUNTING)
and too rare to die.

01:44:58.584 --> 01:45:03.922
(SINGING) There you stood
on the edge of your feather

01:45:04.965 --> 01:45:09.093
Expecting to fly

01:45:13.098 --> 01:45:16.059
DUKE NARRATING:
We're all wired
into a survival trip now.

01:45:16.435 --> 01:45:18.978
No more of the speed
that fueled the '60s.

01:45:19.438 --> 01:45:22.190
That was the fatal flaw
in Tim Leary's trip.

01:45:22.816 --> 01:45:25.610
He crashed
around America, selling
"consciousness expansion"

01:45:25.819 --> 01:45:27.278
without ever giving a thought

01:45:27.363 --> 01:45:29.364
to the grim
meat-hook realities
that were lying in wait

01:45:29.448 --> 01:45:32.200
for all those people
who took him seriously.

01:45:32.993 --> 01:45:34.869
All those pathetically
eager acid freaks

01:45:34.954 --> 01:45:38.540
who thought they could
buy peace and understanding
for three bucks a hit.

01:45:39.250 --> 01:45:41.751
But their loss and failure

01:45:42.127 --> 01:45:43.628
is ours too.

01:45:44.505 --> 01:45:47.549
What Leary took down with him
was the central illusion
of a whole lifestyle

01:45:47.633 --> 01:45:49.175
that he helped create.

01:45:49.760 --> 01:45:52.220
A generation
of permanent cripples,

01:45:52.304 --> 01:45:53.638
failed seekers,

01:45:53.973 --> 01:45:58.017
who never understood
the essential old-mystic
fallacy of the acid culture.

01:45:58.978 --> 01:46:00.436
The desperate assumption

01:46:00.521 --> 01:46:03.731
that somebody
or at least some force

01:46:03.816 --> 01:46:06.568
is tending the light
at the end of the tunnel.

01:46:13.492 --> 01:46:15.910
There was only one road
back to L.A.

01:46:15.995 --> 01:46:18.371
U.S. lnterstate 1 5.

01:46:18.455 --> 01:46:22.375
Just a flat out
high-speed burn through
Baker and Barstow and Berdoo.

01:46:22.835 --> 01:46:24.085
Then onto
the Hollywood Freeway,

01:46:24.169 --> 01:46:25.461
straight into
frantic oblivion,

01:46:25.546 --> 01:46:28.131
safety, obscurity.

01:46:28.215 --> 01:46:31.217
Just another freak
in the freak kingdom.

01:46:31.302 --> 01:46:36.014
(SINGING) I was born
in a cross-fire hurricane

01:46:38.183 --> 01:46:43.688
But l howled at my ma
in the driving rain

01:46:45.274 --> 01:46:49.986
But it's all right now

01:46:50.070 --> 01:46:52.280
ln fact, it's a gas

01:46:52.364 --> 01:46:56.075
But it's all right

01:46:56.160 --> 01:46:59.662
